Package: ALSCL
Title: Age- and Length-Structured Statistical Catch-at-Length Models
Version: 2.4.0
Authors@R: c(person("Hongyu", "Lin", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "linbojun99@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6226-179X")),
             person("Fan", "Zhang", role = "aut", email = "f-zhang@shou.edu.cn",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0214-1790")),
             person("Sisong", "Dong", role = c("aut", "ctb")))
Maintainer: Hongyu Lin <linbojun99@gmail.com>
Description: Fits two stock assessment models to fishery-independent survey
    abundance indices at length using Template Model Builder (TMB). The
    age-structured catch-at-length (ACL) model tracks abundance at age and
    converts it to abundance at length using the probability of length given
    age. The age- and length-structured statistical catch-at-length (ALSCL)
    model tracks abundance by length, age and model time step. Length-specific
    mortality determines survival, and a separate growth transition matrix
    moves survivors between length groups. The package provides multistart
    optimization with optional parallel computation, data preparation and
    checks, sensitivity scenarios, likelihood profiles, deterministic
    projections, fitted-model simulation, hindcast validation, retrospective
    analysis with Mohn's rho, portable assessment archives, diagnostic plots
    and comparisons of model configurations.
